-- int-tests-offence: headline (d), whole scenarios across groups G1 (the entity and whether it is a Jersey entity), G6 (the offences of Articles 19(11) and 20(6)), G7 (Articles 21 to 23, 37 and 38),
-- G8 (Articles 26 and 29) and G9 (the cap in Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f)).  EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from the Law before this module was run:
--   Article 21(3): a Jersey entity that is not a registered charity must not refer to itself, or cause or permit another to refer to it, as a "charity"; 21(10): an entity that contravenes (1), (3) or (5) is liable
--   to a fine of level 3. Article 21(4): a person who, knowing, suspecting or having reasonable grounds to suspect that the entity is a Jersey entity and is not a registered charity, calls it a "charity" intending
--   to induce a gift of property or financial advantage, contravenes (4); 21(9): an entity or other person that contravenes (2), (4) or (6) is liable to imprisonment for 2 years and a fine.
--   Article 37(1): if an offence by a partnership or body corporate is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of a partner, director, governor, secretary or similar officer, that person is also guilty
--   of the offence and liable to the penalty provided for it; the unincorporated association is not named (trap T26).
--   Article 19(11): a person who without reasonable excuse contravenes 19(10) is liable to imprisonment for one year and a fine; Article 20(6): contravening a disqualification order, 2 years and a fine;
--   Article 26(7): 3 months and level 3; Article 26(10): 2 years and a fine; Article 29(1): 2 years and a fine. Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f): Regulations may carry a penalty not exceeding 2 years and a fine.

§ `Integration layer -- headline (d): scenarios`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`a level 3 fine and no imprisonment` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS NOTHING, fine IS `a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`24 months and a fine` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS JUST 24, fine IS `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`12 months and a fine` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS JUST 12, fine IS `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`
GIVETH A `Penalty provided`
`3 months and a level 3 fine` MEANS
    `Penalty provided` WITH `imprisonment up to, in months` IS JUST 3, fine IS `a fine of a level on the standard scale` 3

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      expected IS A LIST OF a
      actual IS A LIST OF a
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the same items` expected actual MEANS
        count expected EQUALS count actual
    AND all (GIVEN x YIELD elem x actual) expected

GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`the unregistered Jersey company` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH
        name IS "Les Pommiers Limited"
        standing IS `not on the register`
        purposes IS LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to relieve poverty in Jersey" `the prevention or relief of poverty`))
        facts IS `Int fx a Jersey company` (LIST (`Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` "P. Gallichan"))
        model IS `Int fx clear model facts`
        people IS LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "P. Gallichan")

GIVETH A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test`
`the facts of a Jersey body for Article 22` MEANS
    `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` WITH `established under` IS `the law of Jersey`, `entitled under that law to refer to itself there as a charity` IS FALSE, `managed wholly or mainly from that jurisdiction` IS FALSE, `specified in an Order under Article 22(4)` IS FALSE

GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`the company calls itself a charity` MEANS
    `a statement about an entity` WITH
        body IS `the unregistered Jersey company`
        `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS `the facts of a Jersey body for Article 22`
        `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS TRUE
        statement IS `Int fx a statement by the entity itself saying` `that it is a “charity”`

GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`the director calls the company a charity knowing it is not` MEANS
    `a statement about an entity` WITH
        body IS `the unregistered Jersey company`
        `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS `the facts of a Jersey body for Article 22`
        `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS TRUE
        statement IS `Int fx a knowing statement by a person that the entity is a charity`

§§ `D1: an unregistered Jersey company calls itself a charity -- the strict offence of Article 21(3)`

-- No knowledge and no intent: only Article 21(3) is contravened; the penalty is a fine of level 3 (Article 21(10)).
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the company calls itself a charity`, officer IS NOTHING))'s `an offence is made out`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the company calls itself a charity`, officer IS NOTHING))'s penalties EQUALS LIST `a level 3 fine and no imprisonment`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the company calls itself a charity`, officer IS NOTHING))'s `every penalty is within the cap of Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the company calls itself a charity`, officer IS NOTHING))'s `the officer is also guilty under Article 37(1)`

§§ `D2: the director calls it a charity, knowing, to get a gift -- Articles 21(3)(b) and 21(4) -- and the director's connivance carries the body's penalty to the director (Article 37(1))`

-- The entity caused or permitted the statement: 21(3)(b) (strict, level 3); the director knows the entity is a Jersey entity and not a registered charity and intends to induce a gift of property: 21(4) (24 months and a fine).
-- F7.4 (favoured): both offences are made out. The body's own offence is 21(3) only (the statement was not made by the entity itself); the director, who connived, is also guilty of THAT offence: level 3.
GIVETH AN `Offence case`
`the offence case of the director and the company` MEANS
    `Offence case` WITH act IS `the director calls the company a charity knowing it is not`, officer IS JUST (`Int fx an officer who connived, of` `a body corporate` `a director of the body corporate`)

#ASSERT `the same items` (LIST `a level 3 fine and no imprisonment`, `24 months and a fine`) ((`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the offence case of the director and the company`)'s penalties)
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the offence case of the director and the company`)'s `the officer is also guilty under Article 37(1)`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the offence case of the director and the company`)'s `the penalties of the officer` EQUALS LIST `a level 3 fine and no imprisonment`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the offence case of the director and the company`)'s `every penalty is within the cap of Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f)`

§§ `D3: the trustee of an unincorporated association who connived is not within Article 37(1) as written (trap T26)`

GIVETH AN `Offence case`
`the offence case of an unincorporated association` MEANS
    `Offence case` WITH act IS `the company calls itself a charity`, officer IS JUST (`Int fx an officer who connived, of` `an unincorporated association` `none of these`)

#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the offence case of an unincorporated association`)'s `the officer is also guilty under Article 37(1)`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the offence case of an unincorporated association`)'s `the penalties of the officer` EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `D4: a governor acts after reporting a reportable matter, without permission -- Article 19(10) -- and without reasonable excuse -- Article 19(11)`

GIVETH A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)`
`the position of a governor who reported on 1 March 2026` MEANS
    `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` WITH
        `the matter arose on` IS YMD 2026 2 20
        `the governor became aware of the matter on` IS YMD 2026 2 22
        `reported to the entity or charity on` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
        `reported to the Commissioner on` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
        `the reports were made promptly` IS TRUE
        `a prompt time has run out` IS TRUE

GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`the governor acts a month after reporting` MEANS
    `acting as a governor after reporting a reportable matter` WITH
        `the entity is a registered charity` IS TRUE
        position IS `the position of a governor who reported on 1 March 2026`
        permissions IS EMPTY
        `the act is done in accordance with any condition on the permission` IS FALSE
        `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS FALSE

-- Reported on 1 March 2026 and acted on 1 April 2026, with no permission: the ban of 19(10) applies. No reasonable excuse: the offence is made out, with 12 months and a fine.
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 4 1) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the governor acts a month after reporting`, officer IS NOTHING))'s `an offence is made out`
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 4 1) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the governor acts a month after reporting`, officer IS NOTHING))'s penalties EQUALS LIST `12 months and a fine`
-- Before the report (28 February 2026) there is no ban.
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 2 28) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the governor acts a month after reporting`, officer IS NOTHING))'s `an offence is made out`
-- With a reasonable excuse, Article 19(11) does not bite.
GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`the governor acts a month after reporting, with a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    `acting as a governor after reporting a reportable matter` WITH
        `the entity is a registered charity` IS TRUE
        position IS `the position of a governor who reported on 1 March 2026`
        permissions IS EMPTY
        `the act is done in accordance with any condition on the permission` IS FALSE
        `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 4 1) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the governor acts a month after reporting, with a reasonable excuse`, officer IS NOTHING))'s `an offence is made out`

§§ `D5, D6, D7: a disqualification order, a demand for information, false information`

#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS (`contravening a disqualification order` WITH contravenes IS TRUE), officer IS NOTHING))'s penalties EQUALS LIST `24 months and a fine`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS (`contravening a disqualification order` WITH contravenes IS FALSE), officer IS NOTHING))'s `an offence is made out`
-- Article 26(7): a requirement validly imposed, not complied with, no privilege, no reasonable excuse: 3 months and level 3.
GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`the person withholds what the Commissioner required` MEANS
    `failing to comply with a requirement under Article 26` WITH facts IS `Facts of a contravention under Article 26(7)` WITH `the requirement was validly imposed under Article 26(1) or (4)` IS TRUE, `the person did what was required` IS FALSE, `what is withheld is subject to legal professional privilege` IS FALSE, `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS FALSE
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the person withholds what the Commissioner required`, officer IS NOTHING))'s penalties EQUALS LIST `3 months and a level 3 fine`
-- Article 26(10): information known to be false in a material particular, intended for an application for registration: 2 years and a fine.
GIVETH AN `Act alleged in the case`
`the person gives false information to the Commissioner` MEANS
    `giving false information under Article 26` WITH facts IS `Facts of providing information under Article 26(10)` WITH `the person provided information to the Commissioner` IS TRUE, `known by the person to be false in a material particular` IS TRUE, `intended for an application for registration` IS TRUE, `intended for deciding whether to serve a required steps notice` IS FALSE, `contained in a document` IS FALSE, `provided under Article 26` IS FALSE
#ASSERT (`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the person gives false information to the Commissioner`, officer IS NOTHING))'s penalties EQUALS LIST `24 months and a fine`

§§ `D8: the day -- the offences of Part 6 begin on 1 January 2019, those of Article 19(11) on 1 May 2018`

-- Article 21 was brought into force with the remainder on 1 January 2019. On 31 December 2018 the gate refuses on the first Article of the list that is not in force, Article 21.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2018 12 31) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the company calls itself a charity`, officer IS NOTHING) BECAUSE "Article 21 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 6) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 January 2019"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30) (`Offence case` WITH act IS `the governor acts a month after reporting`, officer IS NOTHING) BECAUSE "Article 19 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 5) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
